WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.234
♪♪

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:06.234
-Seals don't bark.
Sea lions do.

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:07.534
I said "emu."

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:10.534
I was told
it's pronounced "eem-you."

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.567
This according to our many
Australian viewers,

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:18.367
and I do take their word on it
because they're the experts

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:21.367
in [bleep]
weird-looking animals.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.234
Donald Trump said
he could declassify material

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.200
just by thinking it,
and we made a joke --

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.801
"Great, now Trump
has the shining."

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.634
A bunch of you,

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:33.133
I guess, are fans of the book
"The Shining," and the movie.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:38.434
And you said the actual power
is "the shine."

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:41.667
"The Shining" is just
the name of the book.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.834
Here's an example of one of the
many things that was written.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.334
"The power is called the shine.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.734
It's only the book and movie,
which is called 'The Shining.'

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.767
Also, that's not
how the shine works.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:52.167
You can have mental discussions
with other shine possessors

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.934
and you can see visions
of the past and future.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.133
You can't make things happen.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.868
Plus, that's a different
Big Wheel knock-off

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.467
than the one Danny
has in the film.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.634
Plus plus, Danny isn't
on his Big Wheel knock-off

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:01.968
in that particular scene.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.367
That's the scene
where he walks to room 237

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.133
and is wearing
the Apollo 11 sweater."

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.300
And I just want to say
something about people

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.000
who are super into
the movie "The Shining."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.834
They're not creepy!

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.934
Don't be scared!

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.634
If someone comes over to you
at the dinner party

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:19.968
and talks, you know, about,

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.601
like, intricate details
of "The Shining,"

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:26.100
that doesn't mean they're a bad
person you should be scared of.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.200
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.067
We referenced the White House
Correspondents Dinner

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.767
I did in 2011.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.601
And I said, you know,
that happened when I was a kid.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.200
And one of you kindly
pointed out,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.934
"You were 37 then.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.767
That's old as [bleep]
LOL."

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.400
Which I looked up

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.400
and means "laugh out loud."

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.734
The nerve!

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:57.734
We had a joke about
a Canadian kid

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:01.300
breaking a world record
for the most socks

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.133
put on in 30 seconds

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:06.067
and said it was because

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:08.467
her dad wouldn't let her
touch the thermostat.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:11.567
And the thermostat we showed
was in Fahrenheit.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:13.934
And multiple Canadian viewers

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.234
said that should have been
in Celsius.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.100
But I'd just like to say
to our Canadian viewers,

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.601
you can switch now.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.467
She's gone.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.534
I get it --
you held out,

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:30.033
out of respect.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.567
But she's gone now.

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.100
I respect what you did.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:47.801
Elmer's glue -- apologies --
is not made out of horse,

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:51.634
which we implied
during this week's Ya Burnt.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.801
It is made out of
polyvinyl acetate,

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.734
polyvinyl alcohol,
and polyvinyl glycol.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:59.033
And this is cool.
I looked it up.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.067
Polyvinyl glycol,
if you don't know,

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:05.234
is made of the bones
of Shetland ponies.

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:16.868
Last week's correction
was sponsored by Pizza Hut.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:22.234
And I referenced the fact
that based on how well it went

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.067
and based on the reach
of "Corrections,"

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.434
they would probably be
a bidding war

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:30.567
to see who
this week's sponsor was.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.567
We said Jacques Cousteau...

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:34.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:43.901
We said Jacques Cousteau
had a prank show

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:47.334
in the '60s on Canal+.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:51.667
Canal+ did not exist
until 1984.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:54.100
Until 1975, in fact,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.434
I was told by some of our
French jackals,

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:57.801
France only had one channel.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.968
Only one channel was in France
until 1975.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:03.200
And that's why everyone
in France

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.033
has a mistress.

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:06.200
Or mistress.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.000
Because, you know,
if you'd seen the show

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.734
that was on that night,
you would go --

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:11.901
the only other thing
you could do

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.667
was go have sex
outside the marriage.

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.601
You'd be watching TV
and you'd be like,

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:20.334
[ French accent ]
"Oh, 'Sanford et Fils'?"

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.501
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.334
"Ehh, le homme
de six million dollar?"

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:30.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:32.467
[ Normal voice ]
Fall does not have a solstice.

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:33.801
It has an equinox.

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.901
Spring also doesn't have
a solstice.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:37.901
It has a Planet Fitness.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.400
Baze.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.968
Just stop submitting.

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:50.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:53.033
You don't get -- you just
don't get what this is.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.834
I said you could trust
Wanda Sykes to the point

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:06.667
that if she told you something,
you could take it to the grave.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.734
Everyone corrected me and said
the expression is

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:10.067
"take it to the bank."

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:14.200
I do know what happened,
what went wrong.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.534
I keep my money in a grave.

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:19.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.934
My grandmother's grave.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:28.167
Because, and not to be
too sentimental,

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.834
when I was at her deathbed,

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:34.467
she took my hand, and the last
thing she ever said to me was,

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.467
"I love money!"

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:44.334
[ Sighing ] Oh!

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:45.667
Donald Trump said people
in New York

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:48.000
were walking into stores
with axes,

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.901
and we kind of, you know,
we made light of it.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.267
We were like,
"What are you talking about?"

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:53.400
And then it did turn out
that someone last week

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.567
did walk into a New York City
McDonald's with an ax.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:58.734
And that's terrifying,

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.133
so we're not gonna
make a joke about it.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:04.300
I do want to point out
the New York Post headline.

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.033
They walk a very fine line

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:22.367
over at the New York Post,
where they're like,

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:26.100
"We want to keep people
terrified about crime.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.434
Also, we real good at puns."

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:36.567
That, of course --
he was apprehended.

00:06:36.567 --> 00:06:38.567
By a good guy with an ax.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.234
Just goes to show you.

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:46.067
A man with an ax, of course,

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:49.501
is not the scariest thing
you could see in a McDonald's.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:52.667
Remember our friend here?

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:55.634
So last week I was talking about
this terrifying nightmare,

00:06:55.634 --> 00:06:58.934
and I said his name was
Mack the Knife,

00:06:58.934 --> 00:07:02.434
which is the song
that this character is based on.

00:07:02.434 --> 00:07:05.767
This is Mac Tonight.

00:07:05.767 --> 00:07:10.434
And I did -- I did verify
that is his official name.

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:12.634
That is how it is entered

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.634
in the Epstein flight logs.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.534
♪ If you like French fries ♪

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.234
♪ Come in my basement ♪

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:28.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.734 --> 00:07:35.033
Uh...what have we got here?

00:07:37.234 --> 00:07:38.601
Um...Oh!

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:41.934
So, I'm going to
the Steelers-Jets game

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:43.067
this weekend.

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:45.234
We got a lot of Jets fans
on the crew.

00:07:45.234 --> 00:07:47.067
We make a lot of fun
of the Jets.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:51.000
Steelers are not particularly
off to a hot start this season.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.334
And Kenny Coyle,

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:54.067
one of the guys in the crew,
comes up to me and says,

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:56.367
"I want to make a bet
on the Steelers game."

00:07:56.367 --> 00:07:59.300
And I said, "Sure, whatever,
whatever you want, Kenny."

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.434
And he said,
"If the Jets win,

00:08:01.434 --> 00:08:03.601
you got to mention it
on the show."

00:08:03.601 --> 00:08:05.133
Like, okay, seems pretty...

00:08:05.133 --> 00:08:06.834
Might have done that anyway.

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:09.033
Then he goes,
"And if the Steelers --

00:08:09.033 --> 00:08:10.767
if the Steelers win,

00:08:10.767 --> 00:08:13.767
I'll wear a Steelers
half-shirt on the show."

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:23.968
Just, I mean...

00:08:26.133 --> 00:08:29.467
I think Kenny, like,
wants a certain outcome here.

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:31.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:40.601
"If the Jets win,
you give me a firm handshake.

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:42.934
Steelers win,
I'm putting on my thong."

00:08:42.934 --> 00:08:45.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.834 --> 00:08:55.634
Hey, one of the things
we talked about

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:58.467
in Jokes Seth Can't Tell,
and this was a couple weeks ago,

00:08:58.467 --> 00:09:03.200
was about how some bigoted
people were complaining

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.801
about the new
"Lord of the Rings"

00:09:04.801 --> 00:09:08.300
and the fact that
there were Black actors

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.634
playing some of the hobbits

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:12.868
and someone took issue
with this.

00:09:12.868 --> 00:09:19.534
And I do want to address all
the questions that come across

00:09:19.534 --> 00:09:22.601
our plate here, 'cause this
is a pretty curious one.

00:09:22.601 --> 00:09:24.534
So, let me see here...

00:09:24.534 --> 00:09:26.367
if I can break it down

00:09:26.367 --> 00:09:27.801
and take the time
to break it down

00:09:27.801 --> 00:09:30.767
in a way that maybe
everyone can understand.

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.834
Someone said,
"So, when people have any other

00:09:32.834 --> 00:09:34.634
complaints on bad casting,

00:09:34.634 --> 00:09:37.200
rather it be wrong hair
or eye color, wrong accent,

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.267
or whitewashed roles,
that's all fine.

00:09:39.267 --> 00:09:41.901
But if people have an issue with
Black hobbits, they're bigots?"

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:43.067
Yes.

00:09:43.067 --> 00:09:45.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:57.000
Someone sent this,
and I noticed it too.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.767
The new movie "Blonde"
with Ana de Armas.

00:10:00.767 --> 00:10:03.067
When I was watching, I saw,
there's a line where --

00:10:03.067 --> 00:10:04.400
there's the great
Bobby Cannavale.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:05.767
And he's saying --
I don't know if you can see it,

00:10:05.767 --> 00:10:07.234
but he says,
"I want to protect you

00:10:07.234 --> 00:10:08.868
from all these jackals."

00:10:08.868 --> 00:10:10.534
And someone sent me
a screenshot,

00:10:10.534 --> 00:10:12.434
and I want to just invite
all the jackals --

00:10:12.434 --> 00:10:16.300
if you're ever watching anything
where somebody says "jackal,"

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.133
just take a picture of it
and send it to us.

00:10:18.133 --> 00:10:20.567
And then also,
if you could send --

00:10:20.567 --> 00:10:22.367
if you could write --

00:10:22.367 --> 00:10:23.934
'cause I think we're gonna
edit them all together

00:10:23.934 --> 00:10:25.100
in like a great big thing.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.267
If you'd also write,

00:10:26.267 --> 00:10:30.033
"I give you the legal permission
to use this."

00:10:30.033 --> 00:10:31.701
So then it's on you.

00:10:31.701 --> 00:10:33.400
[ Light laughter ]

00:10:37.701 --> 00:10:40.033
We, um...

00:10:40.033 --> 00:10:42.701
Some Danish documentary
filmmakers were in the news

00:10:42.701 --> 00:10:44.801
and they got interview
by the January 6 committee.

00:10:44.801 --> 00:10:47.133
And yesterday we said, "God,
can you imagine how pleasant

00:10:47.133 --> 00:10:49.767
it was to speak to a Dane?"

00:10:49.767 --> 00:10:52.100
And someone just wrote,
"As a Swede,

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.467
it's never pleasant
to talk to a Dane."

00:10:54.467 --> 00:10:57.334
And it's so funny to me because
I have found this to be true,

00:10:57.334 --> 00:10:58.767
that the countries
of Scandinavia

00:10:58.767 --> 00:11:00.501
are all really [bleep]
to each other.

00:11:00.501 --> 00:11:03.367
And I went on vacation once
and I started a trip --

00:11:03.367 --> 00:11:05.200
I was in Sweden and they said,
"Where are you gonna go?"

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.601
No, excuse me. I was in Denmark.
They said,

00:11:06.601 --> 00:11:07.934
"Where are you gonna go next?"
I said Sweden.

00:11:07.934 --> 00:11:08.968
Everybody in Denmark's like,

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:10.400
"Ugh, why would you go
to Sweden?"

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.634
Then I was in Sweden,
and they said,

00:11:11.634 --> 00:11:13.200
"Where are you gonna go next?"
I said Finland.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.267
And they were like,
"Ugh, Finland's the worst."

00:11:15.267 --> 00:11:17.300
And then when I was in Finland,
I was gonna go to Estonia,

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:19.767
and the Finns were all like,
"Ugh, don't go to Estonia."

00:11:19.767 --> 00:11:22.067
But then I didn't go to Estonia,
'cause I was with Colin Jost

00:11:22.067 --> 00:11:25.300
and he got so [bleep] hungover
that we...

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.701
He was too hungover
to get on a ferry to Estonia.

00:11:28.701 --> 00:11:30.901
So I've never seen Estonia.

00:11:30.901 --> 00:11:32.901
'Cause of Jost.

00:11:32.901 --> 00:11:35.734
Ol' America's sweetheart.

00:11:35.734 --> 00:11:38.868
So I've never seen Tallinn,

00:11:38.868 --> 00:11:40.934
but he gets to be married
to an Avenger.

00:11:40.934 --> 00:11:42.734
[ Light laughter ]

00:11:42.734 --> 00:11:43.934
[ Scoffs ]

00:11:43.934 --> 00:11:45.601
Life.

00:11:47.033 --> 00:11:51.033
We have been hearing from our
international jackals

00:11:51.033 --> 00:11:52.300
how upset they are

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:57.567
that the NBC Store
won't ship internationally.

00:11:57.567 --> 00:12:01.968
Now, in NBC's defense,
we're a very new company.

00:12:01.968 --> 00:12:04.000
[ Laughter ]

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.133
I'm sure the kinks will be
worked out eventually.

00:12:08.133 --> 00:12:10.501
But this is very exciting.

00:12:10.501 --> 00:12:14.000
I'm gonna --
we're gonna do a contest.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.767
If you live in
a foreign country, send --

00:12:16.767 --> 00:12:18.100
I'm gonna give you
an address.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.367
Send a postcard.

00:12:20.367 --> 00:12:22.534
But it has to be a postcard
from your country,

00:12:22.534 --> 00:12:24.400
like with a picture of something
in your country.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:27.334
Has to have the post stamp,
whatever it's called.

00:12:27.334 --> 00:12:28.334
Yeah, right?

00:12:28.334 --> 00:12:30.100
What? Postmark.
Excuse me.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.767
Don't interrupt.

00:12:31.767 --> 00:12:33.901
[ Laughter ]

00:12:33.901 --> 00:12:35.567
I was gonna get there.

00:12:37.968 --> 00:12:40.033
"Hey, I'm part of
'Corrections,' too."

00:12:40.033 --> 00:12:42.534
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.534 --> 00:12:44.868
All next week --
"That was my favorite one."

00:12:44.868 --> 00:12:46.033
Ugh.

00:12:46.033 --> 00:12:47.701
[ Laughter ]

00:12:50.868 --> 00:12:52.334
So, send a postcard.

00:12:52.334 --> 00:12:54.167
International jackals,
send a postcard.

00:12:54.167 --> 00:12:56.167
It's got to have the postmark,
and you have to write on it --

00:12:56.167 --> 00:12:57.300
all you have to write on it --

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.601
obviously,
we need a return address

00:12:58.601 --> 00:12:59.767
because if you win the contest,

00:12:59.767 --> 00:13:01.834
we're gonna send you
a jackal mug.

00:13:01.834 --> 00:13:05.634
You have to write, in your
native tongue, if you'd like,

00:13:05.634 --> 00:13:09.901
"I am a jackal and I don't
deserve your kindness."

00:13:09.901 --> 00:13:11.534
And you can send that
to right here,

00:13:11.534 --> 00:13:16.767
P.O. Box 4748,
New York, New York, 10185.

00:13:16.767 --> 00:13:20.033
And we'll do a drawing,
and maybe you'll be

00:13:20.033 --> 00:13:22.701
a lucky international jackal
to get a mug.

00:13:22.701 --> 00:13:24.534
Well, this was...

00:13:24.534 --> 00:13:26.434
I mean, other than
that one interruption,

00:13:26.434 --> 00:13:29.100
I think, pretty good.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.567
I think, you know,

00:13:30.567 --> 00:13:34.200
if you're rooting
for the Steelers this weekend,

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:39.033
ask yourself what it is
you're hoping to see.

00:13:39.033 --> 00:13:41.868
[ Laughter ]

00:13:41.868 --> 00:13:45.467
And I will see you next week.

